WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.267
-It's always good
to see you, pal.

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.567
-You too.
Thanks for having me.

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:04.934
-Thanks for being here.
Last time, it was on Zoom.

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:07.400
And I appreciate you
just doing that because, really,

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.000
I mean,
you did me a solid there.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.300
You did me a favor.
Thanks for being here.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.167
-Always a treat, man.
-I gotta say, I went to see

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:16.834
the Bond movie on the
big screen, and to hear your --

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:20.033
the theme, "No Time to Die,"
and it was unbelievable.

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:21.734
-Thanks, man.
-It was fantastic.

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.567
-That was cool.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:26.267
-It was beautiful.
Beautifully done.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:29.934
Beautifully shot.
Were you excited?

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:32.634
Eventually -- the movie's
been pushed three times.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:35.734
-I know. We talked about it
when I was here two years ago.

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:37.567
-Yeah.
Daniel Craig came on the show

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:39.234
three times for the same movie.

00:00:39.234 --> 00:00:41.200
[ Laughter ]
It was unbelievable.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.868
-I thought he was buffer
every time he came on.

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.767
-Yeah, he kept getting
in more and more shape.

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:46.968
-By the last time,
he was like -- he was huge.

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:48.400
-He was just -- yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.033
-Yeah, we had nothing
to talk about the third time.

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:51.901
I'm like, "We've already talked
about the whole movie."

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:53.667
-Just showing every clip.
-Yeah, we showed everything.

00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:54.968
-The whole movie in clips.

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:57.100
-But did you get
to go to the premiere?

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.067
-We went to the premiere,
which was at

00:00:58.067 --> 00:00:59.767
the Royal Albert Hall in London.

00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:01.467
-Wait. With the royal family
and everything?

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:03.000
-The royal family, yeah.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.100
-What'd it feel like?
-It was crazy.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.701
We're Americans,
so we're not prepped on all

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:10.334
the sort of customs
with royalty.

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:12.000
And we were told
by our publicist

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.434
right before we went out, like,

00:01:13.434 --> 00:01:15.734
"You don't really
look at them in the eye.

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:19.000
And they talk first.
You don't speak first.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.434
You bow your head."
And then --

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:21.634
Like, this is all real stuff.

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:25.534
And you refer to them
as "Your Royal Highness."

00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:28.234
-Every one of them?
-Yeah. All of --

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:29.868
They're all
"Your Royal Highnesses."

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:31.234
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:32.901
-And so we're like, "Okay."

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:35.200
And then after that, you can say
ma'am or sir or whatever.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.868
And so we're, like, standing
there, we're all nervous.

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:38.934
And they come in,
and they're just like, "Hello."

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:41.667
And they were so casual.
And they, like, shook hands,

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.434
and no one else was doing
the Your Royal Highness stuff.

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:46.601
But we didn't know if that
was 'cause they were English

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:49.234
and we were American,
so we were like -- we were like,

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:51.100
"It's lovely to meet you,
Your Royal Highness."

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.334
[ Laughter ]
Like we whispered --

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:53.567
Like, we were like --
You know what I mean?

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:56.200
-You just kind of tune it out.
But what a treat.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.534
-It's so cool.
-Speaking of other

00:01:58.534 --> 00:02:01.367
English treats,
how is that for a segue?

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:03.534
-I like it.
-You got a --

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:06.334
You won a Grammy
for the second year in a row.

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:07.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:10.934
For Record of the Year.
-Crazy.

00:02:10.934 --> 00:02:14.868
-And presented to you
by the one and only Ringo Starr.

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.434
-I know.
A Beatle.

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:19.934
-What's it like to be handed
a Grammy from a Beatle?

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:22.934
-So, it was the very end
of the ceremony,

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:24.767
which, you've been there --
they're long.

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:25.968
They're many, many --
-Yes.

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:27.767
-They're hours and hours long.
So you're like --

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:29.834
you're hungry at the time.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:32.167
-And at this point,
are you a winner or are you --

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:36.033
-We'd already won a song --
a Grammy way earlier

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:37.868
in the night for the Bond song.
-Yes.

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:39.701
-And this was the final category
of the night.

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:42.501
It was Record of the Year.
I mean, there's always

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:44.501
steep competition,
but this year, it was like,

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:47.467
you know, Megan Thee Stallion,
Beyoncé.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:48.934
[ Cheers ]
It was steep.

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:51.334
And Billie and I
were just like --

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:53.601
just had loved
Megan Thee Stallion so much

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:56.367
that year that we were just
like, "She's gonna sweep.

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:57.701
Like, no question."
-Yeah.

00:02:57.701 --> 00:02:59.767
-And so Ringo walks out.
And I'm like,

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:02.334
"Damn, Megan Thee Stallion
gets to meet Ringo Starr.

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:04.133
That's pretty cool."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:05.400
-"I always wanted to meet him."
Yeah.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.300
-And then they called our name,
and I was like,

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:10.467
"I get to meet Ringo Starr!"
I was so excited.

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:12.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I mean, come on. Right?

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:15.300
And did you --
What did he say?

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.200
Did you talk to him at all?
Did you get to really --

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.400
Did you bond?
-Ringo loves this.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.067
This is, like,
a big Ringo thing.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:23.334
-Of course, "peace and love."
-Peace and love.

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:25.033
-That's right.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:27.601
-And he said -- he said
something really sweet to us.

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:29.334
You know, very casually,
"Congratulations,"

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:31.133
and, you know, whatever,
"Lovely to meet you."

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:33.467
And I said -- I said,
"Aw, man, it's such an honor."

00:03:33.467 --> 00:03:35.067
And he turned,
and he walked away.

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:36.501
[ Laughter ]
Um...

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:38.868
-No, you have to say
"Your Highness" to Ringo Starr.

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:40.100
That's why it happened.
-That's true.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.167
-He was like, "Well,
you don't know the rules."

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:43.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:46.467
-That's true.
-"You don't know the rules."

00:03:46.467 --> 00:03:47.667
Yeah, that's right.
You learn.

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:49.734
You got to live and learn,
right?

00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:53.701
I follow you on the socials,
'cause I think you're very funny

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:56.701
and interesting as well as
a great musician and producer

00:03:56.701 --> 00:03:58.300
and everything,
but you tweet things out

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.467
where I go, like, "Man."

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:01.334
And they just
make me think sometimes.

00:04:01.334 --> 00:04:02.868
They make me laugh
most of the time.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:06.701
-Thanks, man.
-But here's one.

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:07.801
Well, let's just --
There's a couple here.

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:09.767
This one says --
how about this? --

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:11.300
"A funeral but the person
isn't dead,

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.367
and you all just get together
and talk about everything

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:14.534
they've done that annoyed you."

00:04:14.534 --> 00:04:16.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:17.868
Why would you think about that?

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:20.767
-Because I was
thinking about funerals,

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:24.100
and I was thinking about
how everybody just cries

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:27.167
and talks about how wonderful
the person was

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:29.534
and how they were
full of light and love.

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:32.067
And I would be in the back like,

00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:34.334
"Also, one time,
they didn't return my CD."

00:04:34.334 --> 00:04:36.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:37.667
-They all say it --
"They weren't perfect."

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.267
-And so, that's not acceptable

00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:41.200
to do at a funeral,
I don't think.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.634
-Of course.
How about this?

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:46.834
This one here says, "I F'ing
love the subway in New York."

00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:47.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:49.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:52.033
Do you remember doing that?
-I don't know why the actual

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:53.501
New Yorkers in the room clapped

00:04:53.501 --> 00:04:55.701
because the New Yorkers online
booed that tweet.

00:04:55.701 --> 00:04:57.901
They did not
like that tweet at all.

00:04:57.901 --> 00:04:59.334
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:01.501
It's better than
the public transit

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:02.801
in every other city in America.

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:04.300
-This last one here,
I'll just show.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:08.167
This one's a video, because you
posted a lot videos, as well.

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:10.767
He's a good follow, as I said.
-Thanks, man.

00:05:10.767 --> 00:05:13.801
-And this one is not a video
you shot on your phone.

00:05:13.801 --> 00:05:15.567
-No.
-Or a camera or with anyone on.

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:18.467
This was your backyard?
-It's my security camera.

00:05:18.467 --> 00:05:21.534
I was, like,
refilling the pool one day,

00:05:21.534 --> 00:05:23.200
and, like, looked over
and saw something.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:25.167
And I was -- I --
Do you want to just show --

00:05:25.167 --> 00:05:26.267
Do you want
to just show the video?

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:27.467
[ Laughter ]
-I just think it's great.

00:05:27.467 --> 00:05:28.901
Well, no.
I want to set it up

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:32.100
a little bit more because what's
funny is, uh...

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.934
you fell in the pool.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:38.100
And you're talking to Billie.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.300
You're talking to your sister.
-Yeah.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.067
-And you go, "Dude,
the weirdest thing, man.

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:43.133
I fell in the pool today."
-Yeah. That's right.

00:05:43.133 --> 00:05:45.267
-And she goes,
"Did you get it on video?"

00:05:45.267 --> 00:05:46.501
You go --
-I was like,

00:05:46.501 --> 00:05:47.901
"No, I wasn't filming."

00:05:47.901 --> 00:05:48.968
-"I'm not doing this
for a thing."

00:05:48.968 --> 00:05:50.701
-Yeah.
I just -- it was an accident.

00:05:50.701 --> 00:05:52.133
-And she goes --
-She's like,

00:05:52.133 --> 00:05:53.601
"We have security cameras."
-"Check the security camera."

00:05:53.601 --> 00:05:56.067
-"Check the security footage."
-So here's security footage

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:59.000
of Finneas refilling his pool.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.801
Check this out.

00:06:00.801 --> 00:06:02.434
Yeah, there's you.

00:06:02.434 --> 00:06:03.767
-Yeah, holding the hose.
-Yeah.

00:06:03.767 --> 00:06:05.367
-Just doing my job.
-Yeah, just hanging out.

00:06:05.367 --> 00:06:07.667
Yeah.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:12.133
♪♪

00:06:12.133 --> 00:06:13.601
Dude, there's no way.

00:06:13.601 --> 00:06:16.267
You can't act that.
You can't act that.

00:06:16.267 --> 00:06:17.701
It's like...

00:06:17.701 --> 00:06:19.501
'Cause you almost tried
to save yourself at one point.

00:06:19.501 --> 00:06:21.067
-Oh, yeah.
-At one point you're like,

00:06:21.067 --> 00:06:23.033
"I got this.
I'm not going in."

00:06:23.033 --> 00:06:24.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:26.334
So you tried to save yourself,
then you're like, "Oh, man.

00:06:26.334 --> 00:06:28.501
I just went in."
-I totally --

00:06:28.501 --> 00:06:30.000
I was trying to correct.
-Yeah.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.501
-Like I was on ice skates
where you're like,

00:06:31.501 --> 00:06:33.267
"A-ha-ha-ha! Not today."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.267 --> 00:06:35.834
-No, and, gosh,
it was fantastic.

00:06:35.834 --> 00:06:37.634
Thank you
for letting us show that.

00:06:37.634 --> 00:06:39.601
I want to talk about
your debut album, "Optimist."

00:06:39.601 --> 00:06:41.534
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:46.000
-There you go.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.234
You're performing here
on the show tonight...

00:06:48.234 --> 00:06:49.701
-Yeah.
-...which thank you so much.

00:06:49.701 --> 00:06:51.300
-Thanks for having me.
-Which song are you

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.734
playing tonight?
-I'm doing a song called

00:06:52.734 --> 00:06:54.534
"Only a Lifetime" tonight.
[ Cheers ]

00:06:54.534 --> 00:06:56.601
-"Only a Lifetime," tonight.

00:06:56.601 --> 00:06:59.100
And you have
an interesting story

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:02.200
about the first time
you performed on our show.

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:03.400
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.801
-I came for some answers
tonight, if that's okay.

00:07:05.801 --> 00:07:07.434
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:07:07.434 --> 00:07:10.067
-Okay.
So I'll set the scene briefly.

00:07:10.067 --> 00:07:11.734
It's 2018.
-Mm-hmm.

00:07:11.734 --> 00:07:14.868
-I think it was like March 2018.
-Yeah.

00:07:14.868 --> 00:07:17.200
-We get the call.
Billie gets to play

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.534
on the "Tonight Show"
for the first time.

00:07:18.534 --> 00:07:20.801
-Yeah.
-This is a huge deal for us.

00:07:20.801 --> 00:07:23.767
It still is every time, but the
first time is like nothing else.

00:07:23.767 --> 00:07:25.801
-Yeah.
-And so we're super nervous.

00:07:25.801 --> 00:07:27.434
We're excited.
You come in the dressing room.

00:07:27.434 --> 00:07:29.367
You say hi to her.
You're very sweet.

00:07:29.367 --> 00:07:30.968
We go out --
Again, we're like --

00:07:30.968 --> 00:07:32.334
We're not seasoned yet.

00:07:32.334 --> 00:07:34.634
We've only done, like,
one tour so far.

00:07:34.634 --> 00:07:36.467
We're doing her song
"Bellyache."

00:07:36.467 --> 00:07:38.968
It's me.
I was playing acoustic guitar,

00:07:38.968 --> 00:07:41.100
we had a drummer,
and then Billie.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.701
We're all in, like, jumpsuits.
Like --

00:07:43.701 --> 00:07:44.934
Like, we looked like painters.
[ Light laughter ]

00:07:44.934 --> 00:07:47.834
We look like people who paint.
-Yeah.

00:07:47.834 --> 00:07:51.434
-And we're onstage,
we do our song, and I'm like --

00:07:51.434 --> 00:07:52.601
My heart's kind of pounding
through the song.

00:07:52.601 --> 00:07:53.801
-I think it went well.

00:07:53.801 --> 00:07:54.934
-And we felt pretty good
about it.

00:07:54.934 --> 00:07:56.701
We were like,
"You know, we didn't bomb.

00:07:56.701 --> 00:07:58.767
All right."
And you come over,

00:07:58.767 --> 00:08:01.701
and The Roots start jamming,
and they're crushing it.

00:08:01.701 --> 00:08:03.567
You come over.
You're taller

00:08:03.567 --> 00:08:05.801
than I thought you would be.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.801 --> 00:08:08.033
I didn't think you'd be short,
but you're -- he's --

00:08:08.033 --> 00:08:09.534
Like, you're tall, I think,
in my opinion.

00:08:09.534 --> 00:08:11.167
-Yeah, I think --
Well, I'm behind a desk,

00:08:11.167 --> 00:08:14.267
so everyone just kind of assumes
that I'm like about 3 feet tall.

00:08:14.267 --> 00:08:16.133
[ Laughter ]

00:08:16.133 --> 00:08:18.868
I'm like a Muppet.
When they meet me, they're like,

00:08:18.868 --> 00:08:21.868
"Elmo is much taller, yeah."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:24.000
-So, you're taller
than I thought,

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.133
so I'm a little thrown off.
But I'm like, "Great.

00:08:26.133 --> 00:08:27.734
We'll roll with it.
It's fine."

00:08:27.734 --> 00:08:29.701
-Yep.
-"I was expecting shorter.

00:08:29.701 --> 00:08:31.167
It's fine."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:31.167 --> 00:08:33.901
And you're like, you know,
"Good night, everybody!

00:08:33.901 --> 00:08:35.100
Thanks for watching."

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:38.133
The Roots are just killing it,
just rocking out.

00:08:38.133 --> 00:08:40.300
I've watched the show
since you started the show.

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:42.267
I'm so excited,
and I'm clapping.

00:08:42.267 --> 00:08:45.033
I'm looking over, and you guys
do your crescendo at the end.

00:08:45.033 --> 00:08:47.634
-Yeah.
-And I'm just, like, smiling

00:08:47.634 --> 00:08:49.767
and clapping, looking at Quest.

00:08:49.767 --> 00:08:52.234
And Quest he put his sticks
in one hand,

00:08:52.234 --> 00:08:55.567
and he pointed right at me,
and he flipped me the bird.

00:08:55.567 --> 00:08:56.968
[ Laughter ]

00:08:56.968 --> 00:08:58.400
And then --
-Wait. What?

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.267
-And then they all left.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:00.267 --> 00:09:03.067
They all left, and I was
standing there, like, clapping,

00:09:03.067 --> 00:09:04.667
and Questlove,
who I'd never met,

00:09:04.667 --> 00:09:07.534
had just flipped me the bird,
and everybody left.

00:09:07.534 --> 00:09:10.033
-Are you sure I didn't do this?

00:09:10.033 --> 00:09:12.133
-No, that's Ringo, dude.
That's -- Ringo does that.

00:09:12.133 --> 00:09:14.400
-It was not peace or love.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.567
[ Sad trombone plays ]

00:09:15.567 --> 00:09:19.033
-Hey!
-And so I'm shocked.

00:09:19.033 --> 00:09:20.501
And then your producer goes,

00:09:20.501 --> 00:09:22.534
"We're gonna just
do the song one more time."

00:09:22.534 --> 00:09:25.033
And so -- And I think
they aired the second take,

00:09:25.033 --> 00:09:27.801
and we're like --
I looked like I've seen a --

00:09:27.801 --> 00:09:29.434
I look like I've seen a ghost.
-Questlove.

00:09:29.434 --> 00:09:32.133
[ Laughter ]
-And I'm --

00:09:32.133 --> 00:09:35.868
I just -- I'm curious.
-Really?

00:09:35.868 --> 00:09:37.868
Uh...eh...

00:09:37.868 --> 00:09:39.767
[ Laughter ]

00:09:39.767 --> 00:09:41.667
-Never, never, never.

00:09:41.667 --> 00:09:43.601
Guys, Finneas is here.
He would never...

00:09:43.601 --> 00:09:45.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:45.234 --> 00:09:48.167
"Optimist" is out right now.

00:09:48.167 --> 00:09:50.801
Stream it, pick it up
wherever you buy records.

